`3772 passed, 275 skipped, 5 deselected, 1 xfailed, 0 failed` (registry
subset: `332 passed`). Only one existing call site
(`src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py:719`), not the three the task brief
assumed — it passes `version` positionally and is unaffected either way.

Note: because the `_InMemoryStore` fake fully overrides the abstract method,
the four new fake-based tests passed as soon as the fake was updated (before
`base.py`/`store.py`/`RegistryService.py` were touched), rather than failing
with the `TypeError` the brief predicted. See
`.superpowers/sdd/task-1-report.md` for the full account.

# Fix pass 1: code review remediation for commit cb4bddd

## Context

A code review of `cb4bddd` (the task above) raised two Important findings:
the production Lakebase SQL branch for `load_graph_analytics_runs` had no
test coverage of its own (only the `_InMemoryStore` fake was exercised), and
`RegistryService.load_graph_analytics_runs`'s docstring still described the
old version-scoped-only contract. Both are fixed; no production behaviour
changed.

## Changes

1. `tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py` — Added
   `TestLakebaseGraphAnalyticsRunsSql`, driving the real
   `LakebaseRegistryStore.load_graph_analytics_runs` via the existing
   scripted-cursor harness (`_make_lakebase_store` + `_ScriptedCursor` +
   `_ScriptedConn`, following the `_collab_store` pattern — table-ready flag
   short-circuited via `_graph_analytics_runs_ready = True`). Two tests
   assert on the captured `(sql, params)` tuple: `version=None` emits SQL
   without `r.version = %s` and params `("rid-1", "demo", 50)`; `version="1"`
   emits SQL with the predicate and params `("rid-1", "demo", "1", 50)`,
   checked as an exact ordered tuple so a future reordering of the
   `.append()` calls would be caught. Verified this by temporarily swapping
   the append order in `store.py` (limit appended before the version
   predicate) — the new `version="1"` test failed as expected — then
   reverted the swap (confirmed via `git diff` showing no residual change).
2. `src/back/objects/registry/RegistryService.py` — Rewrote the
   `load_graph_analytics_runs` docstring from "Newest-first analytics run
   history for *folder*/*version*." (wrong once `version` is optional) to
   state it spans every version unless `version` scopes it.

## Modified Files

- `tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py`
- `src/back/objects/registry/RegistryService.py`

## Test Result

```bash
env -u DATABRICKS_HOST -u DATABRICKS_TOKEN -u DATABRICKS_CONFIG_PROFILE \
    -u DATABRICKS_CLIENT_ID -u DATABRICKS_CLIENT_SECRET -u LAKEBASE_PROJECT \
    -u LAKEBASE_BRANCH -u LAKEBASE_DATABASE \
    -u LAKEBASE_DATABASE_RESOURCE_SEGMENT -u LAKEBASE_SCHEMA \
    .venv/bin/pytest -q -m "not scenario"
```

`3774 passed, 275 skipped, 5 deselected, 1 xfailed, 0 failed` (full suite);
`tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py`: `72 passed`.

# Task 2: `/dtwin/metrics/history` spans versions

## Context

Continuing the Task 1 work above: the analytics run-history endpoint backing
Knowledge Graph → Management → Runs (a page with no version filter) used to
hard-scope its read to `domain.current_version`, so a domain whose current
version happened to be blank showed an empty history even with rows on file
for earlier versions. The endpoint now spans every version by default and
takes an optional `?version=` to scope back to one, matching the store
contract Task 1 widened.

## Changes

1. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py` — `GET /metrics/history` rewritten:
   added `Query` to the `fastapi` import; the handler now takes
   `version: Optional[str] = Query(default=None)` and
   `limit: int = Query(default=200, ge=1, le=1000)` (default rises from 100
   to 200 to match `/domain/build-runs` — the write cap stays 100 per
   `(domain, version)`, so spanning N versions can yield up to
   `min(limit, 100 × N)` rows and `limit` is now the real bound); the guard
   dropped `or not version` (guarding on version reported an empty history
   whenever `current_version` was blank) and now checks `folder` only; the
   registry call forwards the query `version` (not `domain.current_version`)
   and the query `limit`.
2. `tests/units/dtwin/test_metrics_history.py` (new) — Investigated whether
   this could be a behavioural test instead of the brief's source-text
   assertions (its own caveat: exercising the endpoint needs a session with
   a loaded domain plus a configured registry). Found the existing `client`
   fixture (`TestClient(shared.fastapi.main.app)`) already drives internal
   `/dtwin/*` routes with no domain loaded in `tests/units/api/test_routes.py`
   (`test_neighbors_with_uri_no_domain`), and `get_domain` /
   `RegistryService.from_context` are the only two seams that need a domain
   (both plain module-level names, patchable without touching the endpoint's
   own control flow). Wrote a real behavioural suite driving
   `GET /dtwin/metrics/history` through the FastAPI test client instead of
   reading source text: a no-domain-loaded smoke test needs no mocking at
   all; the domain-loaded cases patch `api.routers.internal.dtwin.get_domain`
   (returns a tiny `_FakeDomain` with `uc_domain_folder` set and
   `current_version=""`) and
   `back.objects.registry.RegistryService.RegistryService.from_context`
   (returns a `_FakeRegistryService` recording each call, mirroring the
   brief's `_FakeService`). Covers: omitting `version` forwards `None` to the
   registry even when `current_version` is blank (the regression this task
   fixes); an explicit `?version=` is still forwarded; the default `limit` is
   200 and an explicit `?limit=` is forwarded; `limit` outside `[1, 1000]`
   is rejected with 422. No source-text assertions were needed or kept.

## Modified Files

- `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
- `tests/units/dtwin/test_metrics_history.py` (new)

